From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:26:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] net: stmmac: dwmac-sun8i: Limit TX checksum insertion to
 2032 bytes

On an Allwinner H616, the EMAC inserts wrong checksums into frames
longer than 2032 bytes, and sometimes corrupts the frame sent after
such a frame. In MAC loopback at MTU 4070, with checksum insertion on:
- UDP frames of 2036 and 2040 bytes: 0 of 40 had valid checksums (the
  payload was intact);
- 2044-byte UDP frames checksummed in software, sent right after them:
  4 of 20 intact;
- 2054-byte raw frames: 1 of 30 had 2 bytes changed at offset 24.
2032-byte UDP frames at MTU 2018 were fine. With checksum insertion
off, all of these frames were intact.

Add tx_coe_max_len to plat_stmmacenet_data, the longest frame (without
the FCS) the TX checksum engine handles. stmmac_fix_features() turns
TX checksum offload off for MTUs that allow longer frames, and
stmmac_features_check() asks for software checksums for longer frames,
which VLAN tags can still produce below that MTU.

Set it to 2032 bytes for dwmac-sun8i, which keeps checksum offload up to
MTU 2018.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c | 4 ++++
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c | 9 +++++++++
 include/linux/stmmac.h                            | 2 ++
 3 files changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c
index 3de46f8..33ec037 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c
@@ -227,6 +227,9 @@ static const struct emac_variant emac_variant_h6 = {
 /* Used in TX_CTL0 */
 #define EMAC_TX_TRANSMITTER_EN  BIT(31)
 
+/* TX checksum insertion corrupts longer frames, and others sent after them */
+#define EMAC_TX_COE_MAX_LEN	2032
+
 /* Used in EMAC_TX_FLOW_CTL */
 #define EMAC_TX_FLOW_CTL_EN             BIT(0)
 
@@ -1261,6 +1264,7 @@ static int sun8i_dwmac_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	 */
 	plat_dat->rx_coe = STMMAC_RX_COE_TYPE2;
 	plat_dat->tx_coe = true;
+	plat_dat->tx_coe_max_len = EMAC_TX_COE_MAX_LEN;
 	plat_dat->flags |= STMMAC_FLAG_HAS_SUN8I;
 	plat_dat->bsp_priv = gmac;
 	plat_dat->init = sun8i_dwmac_init;
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
index 466c711..101df45 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
@@ -5073,6 +5073,11 @@ static netdev_features_t stmmac_features_check(struct sk_buff *skb,
 	    !stmmac_has_ip_ethertype(skb))
 		features &= ~(NETIF_F_IP_CSUM | NETIF_F_IPV6_CSUM);
 
+	/* VLAN tags can make a frame longer than the MTU allows for */
+	if (priv->plat->tx_coe_max_len &&
+	    skb->len > priv->plat->tx_coe_max_len)
+		features &= ~NETIF_F_CSUM_MASK;
+
 	if (skb_is_gso(skb)) {
 		if (!stmmac_tso_channel_permitted(priv, queue) ||
 		    !stmmac_tso_valid_packet(skb))
@@ -6265,6 +6270,10 @@ static netdev_features_t stmmac_fix_features(struct net_device *dev,
 	if (priv->plat->bugged_jumbo && (dev->mtu > ETH_DATA_LEN))
 		features &= ~NETIF_F_CSUM_MASK;
 
+	if (priv->plat->tx_coe_max_len &&
+	    dev->mtu + ETH_HLEN > priv->plat->tx_coe_max_len)
+		features &= ~NETIF_F_CSUM_MASK;
+
 	if (priv->plat->core_type == DWMAC_CORE_XGMAC) {
 		if (features & NETIF_F_HW_VLAN_CTAG_RX)
 			features |= NETIF_F_HW_VLAN_STAG_RX;
diff --git a/include/linux/stmmac.h b/include/linux/stmmac.h
index 4430b96..7075395 100644
--- a/include/linux/stmmac.h
+++ b/include/linux/stmmac.h
@@ -257,6 +257,8 @@ struct plat_stmmacenet_data {
 	bool force_thresh_dma_mode;
 	bool riwt_off;
 	int rx_coe;
+	/* Longest frame (without FCS) for TX checksum insertion, 0: any */
+	unsigned int tx_coe_max_len;
 	int max_speed;
 	int maxmtu;
 	int multicast_filter_bins;
